{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The oriented incidence matrix of a directed hypergraph. Entry (v, p) is −1 when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" is a source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of column "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":", +1 when it is a target, and 0 otherwise."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This is the matrix of Gallo, Longo, Pallottino and Nguyen (1993). A directed graph’s edge is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"column with one source and one target, which gives the oriented incidence matrix of spectral","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L). The matrix conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedHypergraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hypergraphs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged. It is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not a ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Two-bit-planes","text":"Two bit planes","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The sources and the targets are each stored as an ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a vertex can be on both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sides of a column. Its entry is then target − source = 0, with both bits kept.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"sources(ofHyperedgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"targets(ofHyperedgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the stars and equality read the planes,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so nothing is lost. A directed self-loop is such a column. ","type":"text"},{"code":"reversed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" swaps the planes, negating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every entry, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"transposed()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" transposes each plane to give the dual. Both are O(1).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage is 4·n·m\/8 bytes, so the matrix suits dense or small incidence. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":" is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sparse representation. Equality compares both planes cell for cell, with equal shape, so column"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order counts."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init()","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-1k5cq","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-46tuh","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-6qyfl","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-y850","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init(vertexCount:)","doc:\/\/Incide